FLASH ATTENTION COMPATIBILITY CHECK
================================================================================

1. System Information:
   PyTorch version: 2.5.1+cu124
   CUDA version (PyTorch built with): 12.4
   CUDNN version: 90100
   GPU: NVIDIA RTX A6000
   GPU Compute Capability: 8.6
   GPU Memory: 47.5 GB

2. GPU Architecture Analysis:
   Quadro RTX 8000 is based on Turing architecture (compute capability 7.5)
   Flash Attention requirements:
   - Compute capability >= 7.0 (Volta) for Flash Attention v1
   - Compute capability >= 8.0 (Ampere) for Flash Attention v2 optimal performance
   Your GPU compute capability: 8.6

3. Testing Scaled Dot Product Attention Kernels:

   Testing FP16 (seq_len=4096):
   ✓ Flash Attention: AVAILABLE
   ✓ Memory Efficient Attention: AVAILABLE
   ✓ Math Attention: AVAILABLE

   Testing BF16 (seq_len=4096):
   ✓ Flash Attention: AVAILABLE
   ✓ Memory Efficient Attention: AVAILABLE
   ✓ Math Attention: AVAILABLE

4. PyTorch Backend Query (for reference):
   Note: These functions check if kernels CAN be built, not if they're optimal for your tensors
   torch.backends.cuda.flash_sdp_enabled(): True
   torch.backends.cuda.mem_efficient_sdp_enabled(): True
   torch.backends.cuda.math_sdp_enabled(): True

5. Specific Configuration Issues:
   BF16 + Flash Attention on Turing (7.5):
   - Flash Attention v1 has limited BF16 support on Turing
   - BF16 is better supported on Ampere (8.0+) and newer
   - Memory Efficient kernel may work better for BF16 on Turing

